1
00:01:42,440 --> 00:01:44,600
NEW MESSAGE

2
00:01:51,520 --> 00:01:53,200
<i>There's a campground nearby.</i>

3
00:01:53,280 --> 00:01:55,720
<i>I'll wait for you there.</i>
<i>There's something I need to tell you.</i>

4
00:02:26,960 --> 00:02:30,360
ZHUANG NING

5
00:02:33,320 --> 00:02:34,720
ZHUANG NING

6
00:02:39,880 --> 00:02:42,800
<i>Hello, the number you have dialed</i>
<i>is powered off.</i>

7
00:03:08,120 --> 00:03:09,560
GO STRAIGHT 102 M

8
00:03:36,080 --> 00:03:39,200
VISITOR REST AREA

9
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:50,280
Zhuang Ning.

10
00:03:53,080 --> 00:03:54,120
Zhuang Ning!

11
00:04:03,320 --> 00:04:05,880
<i>Hello, the number you have dialed</i>
<i>is powered off.</i>

12
00:04:54,120 --> 00:04:56,320
- Zheng Yu.
- What are you doing here?

13
00:04:57,920 --> 00:04:59,680
I was about to ask you the same thing.

14
00:04:59,760 --> 00:05:04,680
TWENTY MINUTES AGO

15
00:05:07,160 --> 00:05:08,560
<i>What's the matter?</i>

16
00:05:08,640 --> 00:05:09,840
<i>It's already late.</i>

17
00:05:09,920 --> 00:05:11,640
<i>Whatever it is, tell me when you get back.</i>

18
00:05:13,360 --> 00:05:14,760
I HURT MY FOOT, YOU…

19
00:06:38,720 --> 00:06:41,800
<i>Hello, the number you have dialed</i>
<i>is powered off.</i>

20
00:07:00,080 --> 00:07:01,480
Your gear is surprisingly complete.

21
00:07:03,520 --> 00:07:05,240
Since you couldn't reach Zhuang Ning,

22
00:07:05,320 --> 00:07:07,440
why didn't you ask the group leader
to help look for her?

23
00:07:08,680 --> 00:07:10,600
I'm not even sure
if Zhuang Ning is missing.

24
00:07:11,560 --> 00:07:13,520
And she's not the type
to send messages randomly.

25
00:07:14,640 --> 00:07:17,640
What if something really happened
and she wanted to talk to me in private?

26
00:07:18,400 --> 00:07:22,240
Besides, this is a developed tourist area.
It's not that dangerous.

27
00:07:22,960 --> 00:07:24,400
Since you turned her down,

28
00:07:25,040 --> 00:07:27,720
maybe she saw your message
and decided not to come.

29
00:07:27,800 --> 00:07:29,600
Or maybe you just
missed each other on the way.

30
00:07:30,960 --> 00:07:32,000
That's possible.

31
00:07:37,840 --> 00:07:39,440
Did you bump into something?
Let me see.

32
00:07:39,520 --> 00:07:40,360
I'm fine.

33
00:07:48,320 --> 00:07:49,720
It's just a minor scrape.

34
00:07:49,800 --> 00:07:51,000
Wait.

35
00:07:52,400 --> 00:07:53,760
This scar…

36
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:56,400
How did you get it?

37
00:07:58,880 --> 00:08:01,880
After high school graduation, I got into
a fight with someone. It left a scar.

38
00:08:04,160 --> 00:08:05,040
You get into fights?

39
00:08:06,520 --> 00:08:08,240
I fought back when someone beat me up.

40
00:08:08,920 --> 00:08:10,360
I guess that counts as a fight.

41
00:08:12,400 --> 00:08:13,440
Who beat you up?

42
00:08:14,920 --> 00:08:15,800
Debt collectors.

43
00:08:19,640 --> 00:08:21,240
Those two at the hospital last time?

44
00:08:23,240 --> 00:08:26,240
My uncle was the one
who introduced them to me.

45
00:08:26,320 --> 00:08:28,160
<i>I was naïve back then.</i>

46
00:08:28,240 --> 00:08:29,880
<i>I believed he genuinely wanted to help me,</i>

47
00:08:29,960 --> 00:08:31,560
<i>only to realize later that</i>

48
00:08:31,640 --> 00:08:33,919
<i>the more money he gave me,</i>
<i>the more I owed.</i>

49
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:37,840
<i>But my mom's surgery failed,</i>
<i>and I couldn't pay them back.</i>

50
00:08:45,200 --> 00:08:48,480
Dodge! Come on, dodge!

51
00:08:49,160 --> 00:08:50,840
Dodge!

52
00:09:32,560 --> 00:09:34,880
Next time you can't call the group leader,

53
00:09:36,040 --> 00:09:37,000
just call me instead.

54
00:09:40,760 --> 00:09:42,240
At least now,

55
00:09:43,920 --> 00:09:45,920
we can call ourselves friends, right?

56
00:11:20,200 --> 00:11:21,080
Zheng Yu.

57
00:11:23,560 --> 00:11:24,400
Zheng Yu.

58
00:11:35,520 --> 00:11:36,960
The rain's stopped. Let's head back.

59
00:12:09,840 --> 00:12:12,360
You're here early.
It's not time for class yet.

60
00:12:13,360 --> 00:12:14,640
That's right.

61
00:12:14,720 --> 00:12:17,560
I just woke up with nothing to do,
so I wanted to read for a bit.

62
00:12:18,720 --> 00:12:20,080
As expected of a top university!

63
00:12:20,160 --> 00:12:22,640
One of your classmates
stayed up all night writing a report here.

64
00:12:22,720 --> 00:12:24,560
She didn't even realize
the door had been locked.

65
00:12:24,640 --> 00:12:27,680
I only let her out
when I came to clean this morning.

66
00:12:27,760 --> 00:12:29,800
- Stayed up writing a report?
- That's right.

67
00:12:30,960 --> 00:12:33,600
University students these days
really have it tough.

68
00:12:35,040 --> 00:12:36,240
They sure do.

69
00:12:37,240 --> 00:12:38,720
I'll let you get back to work, ma'am.

70
00:12:39,560 --> 00:12:42,520
I'll go check the kitchen
to see if breakfast is ready.

71
00:12:47,720 --> 00:12:49,840
You go in first, and I'll follow you.

72
00:12:54,280 --> 00:12:56,880
ACADEMIC BUILDING

73
00:13:13,120 --> 00:13:13,960
Go on.

74
00:13:28,960 --> 00:13:31,600
Did you go to the campground last night?

75
00:13:32,520 --> 00:13:33,440
The campground?

76
00:13:33,520 --> 00:13:36,920
You texted me to meet you there
because you had something to tell me.

77
00:13:37,520 --> 00:13:38,920
I went,

78
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:40,120
but I didn't see you there.

79
00:13:41,520 --> 00:13:42,360
<i>Your phone.</i>

80
00:13:45,360 --> 00:13:46,400
Let me borrow it.

81
00:13:51,280 --> 00:13:52,480
Are you listening to me?

82
00:13:53,600 --> 00:13:56,280
Did anything happen to you last night?

83
00:13:57,680 --> 00:13:59,080
No. What about you?

84
00:14:02,840 --> 00:14:04,960
Xie Yudi always used to know
where I was in the past.

85
00:14:06,320 --> 00:14:08,080
You were the one telling him, right?

86
00:14:08,160 --> 00:14:09,560
<i>I don't like that.</i>

87
00:14:12,960 --> 00:14:17,280
I was going to the campground last night,

88
00:14:18,080 --> 00:14:22,120
but I accidentally fell asleep
in the activity room.

89
00:14:22,720 --> 00:14:27,160
Then it started raining outside,
so I didn't go.

90
00:14:27,760 --> 00:14:30,000
And my phone was out of battery too.

91
00:14:30,640 --> 00:14:32,600
So what were you originally
planning to tell me?

92
00:14:32,680 --> 00:14:36,080
I… I wanted to say…

93
00:14:41,760 --> 00:14:46,760
I lost some of the plants
we were using for the specimens yesterday.

94
00:14:46,840 --> 00:14:47,680
I'm sorry.

95
00:14:48,400 --> 00:14:51,360
Why did you need to meet me outside
just to tell me that?

96
00:14:53,760 --> 00:14:54,720
Because…

97
00:14:57,400 --> 00:14:58,280
Because…

98
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:01,840
Forget it.

99
00:15:02,720 --> 00:15:03,640
It's fine.

100
00:15:06,680 --> 00:15:09,760
ANTIDIARRHEAL TABLETS

101
00:15:26,680 --> 00:15:27,920
<i>- Zhou Ren.</i>
<i>- Here.</i>

102
00:15:29,680 --> 00:15:31,440
- Zhang Qi.
- Here.

103
00:15:32,560 --> 00:15:34,080
- Chen Yanzhou.
- Here.

104
00:15:34,960 --> 00:15:36,920
- Zheng Yu.
- Here.

105
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:38,280
Zhuang Ning.

106
00:15:41,360 --> 00:15:42,280
Is Zhuang Ning here?

107
00:15:44,160 --> 00:15:46,400
It rained all night yesterday.

108
00:15:46,480 --> 00:15:48,360
For everyone's safety,

109
00:15:48,440 --> 00:15:50,640
we decided at the last minute
to hold class at the base.

110
00:15:51,240 --> 00:15:52,720
But none of you

111
00:15:52,800 --> 00:15:55,240
should be slacking off
just because we're having the class here.

112
00:15:55,320 --> 00:15:58,480
- Where's Zhuang Ning?
- I don't know.

113
00:16:04,080 --> 00:16:06,280
All right, that's all for today.
Class dismissed.

114
00:16:07,640 --> 00:16:10,040
Wait, hold on a second!

115
00:16:10,120 --> 00:16:11,400
Don't rush off, everyone.

116
00:16:11,480 --> 00:16:12,600
Here's the thing.

117
00:16:13,120 --> 00:16:16,640
The lecturers just discussed it,
and we're planning an activity

118
00:16:16,720 --> 00:16:18,880
to make up for not being able
to get out in the field today.

119
00:16:18,960 --> 00:16:23,280
So I've prepared
a few little games for you.

120
00:16:23,360 --> 00:16:25,360
The lecturers will chip in

121
00:16:25,440 --> 00:16:27,920
to prepare some red envelopes
for the winners.

122
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:28,880
- Nice!
- Nice!

123
00:16:28,960 --> 00:16:32,160
So I hope everyone will
participate this afternoon, all right?

124
00:16:32,240 --> 00:16:34,760
- All right!
- All right!

125
00:16:34,840 --> 00:16:36,520
But. But!

126
00:16:36,600 --> 00:16:38,960
After lunch, we still have two classes.

127
00:16:40,480 --> 00:16:43,320
Our activity starts at four, okay?

128
00:16:43,400 --> 00:16:44,600
Four o'clock.

129
00:16:44,680 --> 00:16:47,520
- Okay.
- Don't leave us hanging!

130
00:16:47,600 --> 00:16:50,520
Just leave the phone here.
Someone will come looking for it.

131
00:16:51,600 --> 00:16:53,440
Or ask the students.

132
00:16:53,520 --> 00:16:54,960
You there.

133
00:16:55,640 --> 00:16:56,600
Come here.

134
00:16:58,960 --> 00:17:02,400
Our cleaning lady
found a phone in the activity room.

135
00:17:02,480 --> 00:17:04,680
It's been there all morning,
but no one's claimed it.

136
00:17:04,760 --> 00:17:07,040
Could you take a photo
and post it in the class group chat?

137
00:17:11,040 --> 00:17:13,079
This phone looks like my roommate's.

138
00:17:13,160 --> 00:17:16,119
She was in the activity room last night,
so she must've left it there.

139
00:17:16,200 --> 00:17:17,119
Last night?

140
00:17:17,200 --> 00:17:20,040
Do you mean the girl
who got locked inside the activity room?

141
00:17:20,119 --> 00:17:21,640
What do you mean?

142
00:17:21,720 --> 00:17:24,040
There was a girl
studying in there last night.

143
00:17:24,119 --> 00:17:25,920
She accidentally got locked inside.

144
00:17:26,599 --> 00:17:28,880
Who was the last person
to check the room yesterday?

145
00:17:28,960 --> 00:17:30,080
Was it you?

146
00:17:30,160 --> 00:17:31,680
Didn't you see her?

147
00:17:31,760 --> 00:17:32,800
That can't be right.

148
00:17:33,400 --> 00:17:35,360
When I locked up, there was no one inside.

149
00:17:36,800 --> 00:17:39,040
Then a guy came by to borrow the key.

150
00:17:39,120 --> 00:17:41,160
He said he'd left something inside.

151
00:17:41,240 --> 00:17:43,080
But he didn't notice
anyone in there either.

152
00:17:43,160 --> 00:17:44,760
ACADEMIC BUILDING

153
00:18:30,960 --> 00:18:32,560
All right. Everyone, settle down.

154
00:18:32,640 --> 00:18:34,400
Listen up.

155
00:18:34,480 --> 00:18:37,240
Since we have limited facilities up here,

156
00:18:37,320 --> 00:18:40,360
I've arranged a simple game
for everyone to play.

157
00:18:40,440 --> 00:18:42,400
It's dodgeball.

158
00:18:42,480 --> 00:18:43,600
See these balloons?

159
00:18:43,680 --> 00:18:44,920
They're filled with water.

160
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:47,640
- So today--
- I barely brought any clothes.

161
00:18:47,720 --> 00:18:49,760
- Yes, same here!
- Same here!

162
00:18:50,400 --> 00:18:52,160
It's fine. The water's perfectly clean.

163
00:18:52,240 --> 00:18:54,520
I got it straight from the restroom.

164
00:18:54,600 --> 00:18:55,520
Look at him!

165
00:18:55,600 --> 00:18:58,080
Now, let me explain the rules.

166
00:18:58,160 --> 00:19:02,520
Each girl can choose a guy
to play dodgeball with.

167
00:19:02,600 --> 00:19:07,080
You can decide among yourselves
who throws and who dodges.

168
00:19:07,160 --> 00:19:09,160
So the person dodging

169
00:19:09,240 --> 00:19:12,520
must stay inside this circle
while dodging.

170
00:19:12,600 --> 00:19:16,720
The thrower gets five attempts
from the circle opposite.

171
00:19:16,800 --> 00:19:21,320
If the thrower hits the person dodging
three times or more,

172
00:19:21,400 --> 00:19:23,160
the thrower wins a red envelope.

173
00:19:23,240 --> 00:19:24,600
The red envelope is right there!

174
00:19:24,680 --> 00:19:26,760
I have no idea how much is in it either,
but it's a lot!

175
00:19:28,640 --> 00:19:30,240
So anyway,

176
00:19:30,320 --> 00:19:32,840
if the dodger avoids three or more hits,

177
00:19:32,920 --> 00:19:34,600
they will get a red envelope.

178
00:19:34,680 --> 00:19:35,520
Everyone understand?

179
00:19:35,600 --> 00:19:37,080
- Got it!
- Let's get started!

180
00:19:37,160 --> 00:19:38,880
All right, let's begin!

181
00:19:38,960 --> 00:19:40,400
- Yes!
- Let's go!

182
00:19:40,480 --> 00:19:41,640
Who's going first?

183
00:19:41,720 --> 00:19:42,920
Let's go by student number.

184
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:46,360
- Me!
- Class 1!

185
00:19:46,440 --> 00:19:48,240
- Class 2!
- Let's go with Class 2!

186
00:19:48,960 --> 00:19:50,720
- Send someone up.
- Linlin.

187
00:19:50,800 --> 00:19:51,640
Go on!

188
00:19:52,280 --> 00:19:53,560
Let's go!

189
00:19:53,640 --> 00:19:56,080
- Go!
- I'm sending you down.

190
00:19:56,160 --> 00:19:57,560
Linlin!

191
00:19:57,640 --> 00:19:58,920
You got this!

192
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:00,680
Everyone, a round of applause!

193
00:20:02,160 --> 00:20:03,200
Linlin, who will you pick?

194
00:20:05,760 --> 00:20:07,600
- How about you?
- Me?

195
00:20:07,680 --> 00:20:09,520
- Good!
- Good!

196
00:20:09,600 --> 00:20:10,440
All right!

197
00:20:12,800 --> 00:20:13,840
Come on.

198
00:20:14,840 --> 00:20:16,440
You got this, Linlin!

199
00:20:28,240 --> 00:20:29,320
Zhang Qi.

200
00:20:29,400 --> 00:20:31,520
Did you sneak in some practice
while preparing the props?

201
00:20:32,600 --> 00:20:34,360
Then I won't hold back.

202
00:20:35,080 --> 00:20:36,720
All right, next up!

203
00:20:38,120 --> 00:20:39,280
I'll go!

204
00:20:45,360 --> 00:20:48,080
- You got this!
- You got this!

205
00:20:59,480 --> 00:21:00,440
Sorry, sir!

206
00:21:01,040 --> 00:21:02,040
Go for it!

207
00:21:05,480 --> 00:21:07,000
You got this!

208
00:21:07,080 --> 00:21:10,240
- You can do it!
- You got this!

209
00:21:10,320 --> 00:21:11,320
Come on!

210
00:21:11,400 --> 00:21:14,480
You got this!

211
00:21:24,120 --> 00:21:24,960
Good job!

212
00:21:25,040 --> 00:21:27,040
- Well done!
- All right, next up!

213
00:21:34,680 --> 00:21:37,240
- This guy is relentless!
- Not gentlemanly at all!

214
00:21:37,320 --> 00:21:38,880
Exactly!

215
00:21:44,920 --> 00:21:45,920
Pick me.

216
00:21:46,000 --> 00:21:48,120
That way, no matter who wins,
we'll get the red envelope.

217
00:21:49,680 --> 00:21:51,120
Don't you believe we both can win?

218
00:22:01,080 --> 00:22:02,840
Come on, girls!

219
00:22:02,920 --> 00:22:05,720
Work harder, or the boys
will take all the red envelopes!

220
00:22:05,800 --> 00:22:07,400
It's all down to skill!

221
00:22:07,480 --> 00:22:09,560
Next up, Zheng Yu.

222
00:22:10,360 --> 00:22:12,040
Come on, Zheng Yu!

223
00:22:12,120 --> 00:22:14,720
- Come on!
- You got this!

224
00:22:14,800 --> 00:22:15,960
Who will you pick?

225
00:22:19,920 --> 00:22:21,120
Xie Yudi.

226
00:22:24,480 --> 00:22:25,640
She picked him?

227
00:22:25,720 --> 00:22:28,120
What's going on?
Is your luck finally turning around?

228
00:22:28,760 --> 00:22:30,680
Seriously?

229
00:22:30,760 --> 00:22:32,400
So do you want to throw or dodge?

230
00:22:38,040 --> 00:22:44,240
- Go for it!
- Go for it!

231
00:22:44,320 --> 00:22:47,840
- Go for it!
- You can do this!

232
00:22:48,480 --> 00:22:49,880
- Come on!
- You got this!

233
00:22:49,960 --> 00:22:52,360
- Go for it!
- Go for it!

234
00:22:56,400 --> 00:22:57,920
Oh gosh.

235
00:23:00,800 --> 00:23:02,440
Zheng Yu!

236
00:23:04,200 --> 00:23:06,480
Hey, Xie Yudi. Don't go easy on her!

237
00:23:06,560 --> 00:23:08,200
Yes, don't hold back!

238
00:23:28,000 --> 00:23:30,120
- Go for it, Zheng Yu!
- Hey, Xie Yudi!

239
00:23:30,200 --> 00:23:31,160
I've figured it out.

240
00:23:31,240 --> 00:23:33,600
Don't just move your upper body.
You need to move your feet too!

241
00:23:33,680 --> 00:23:34,920
That's right!

242
00:23:35,000 --> 00:23:35,840
Got it.

243
00:23:36,400 --> 00:23:37,360
It's just a game.

244
00:23:51,720 --> 00:23:54,080
Yes! We've hit him three times!

245
00:23:54,160 --> 00:23:57,880
- Zheng Yu wins!
- She won!

246
00:23:57,960 --> 00:23:59,840
- Zheng Yu! Zheng Yu!
- Should we keep going?

247
00:23:59,920 --> 00:24:01,000
Of course!

248
00:24:01,080 --> 00:24:02,760
Everyone's already thrown all five balls.

249
00:24:02,840 --> 00:24:07,280
Keep going! Keep going! Keep going!

250
00:24:51,040 --> 00:24:54,800
- We take the win!
- Zheng Yu!

251
00:24:54,880 --> 00:24:57,240
Zheng Yu!

252
00:24:58,880 --> 00:25:01,840
Zheng Yu!

253
00:25:03,320 --> 00:25:05,360
Zheng Yu, you won!

254
00:25:06,040 --> 00:25:07,000
Zheng Yu!

255
00:25:07,080 --> 00:25:08,960
Xie Yudi, the water's really clean.

256
00:25:09,040 --> 00:25:10,600
It's safe to drink. It's fine.

257
00:25:10,680 --> 00:25:13,200
Zheng Yu!

258
00:25:14,640 --> 00:25:16,560
That was amazing!

259
00:25:16,640 --> 00:25:20,160
- Zheng Yu!
- She's incredible!

260
00:25:26,600 --> 00:25:32,400
Zheng Yu! Zheng Yu! Zheng Yu!

261
00:26:12,800 --> 00:26:13,880
What's wrong?

262
00:26:15,880 --> 00:26:16,880
You're burning up.

263
00:26:17,880 --> 00:26:20,080
Let's go to the hospital.
I'll call the group leader.

264
00:26:21,080 --> 00:26:22,400
Bo's luck is unbelievably bad.

265
00:26:22,480 --> 00:26:25,600
- Someone's coming.
- As if your luck was any better.

266
00:26:30,560 --> 00:26:31,760
Let's play another round later.

267
00:26:31,840 --> 00:26:33,400
- I can't believe this.
- We'll see later.

268
00:26:33,480 --> 00:26:34,600
It's Zhang Qi.

269
00:26:36,240 --> 00:26:37,400
Who are you sharing a room with?

270
00:26:38,960 --> 00:26:39,800
I…

271
00:26:42,080 --> 00:26:43,560
Chen Yanzhou.

272
00:26:43,640 --> 00:26:45,000
We're going out to eat.

273
00:26:45,080 --> 00:26:47,560
There's a farmhouse restaurant nearby.
Want to come with us?

274
00:26:51,920 --> 00:26:52,920
That's strange.

275
00:26:53,000 --> 00:26:55,040
He's not in the room
or out in the courtyard.

276
00:26:56,040 --> 00:26:57,160
Where else could he be?

277
00:26:57,760 --> 00:26:58,760
I'll go check inside.

278
00:26:58,840 --> 00:27:00,680
You're sharing a room with Zhang Qi?

279
00:27:06,040 --> 00:27:07,760
Where's my key card?

280
00:27:09,120 --> 00:27:10,480
Did I leave it in the room?

281
00:27:11,920 --> 00:27:13,760
I'll get another one from the front desk.

282
00:27:14,440 --> 00:27:17,960
Maybe he's in the room,
but he just doesn't want to deal with you.

283
00:27:18,040 --> 00:27:20,280
Everyone supported
the game you organized this afternoon,

284
00:27:20,360 --> 00:27:21,640
but he was nowhere to be seen.

285
00:27:21,720 --> 00:27:24,400
If he's too good to hang out with us,
why bother chasing after him?

286
00:27:25,480 --> 00:27:27,400
Don't say it like that.

287
00:27:27,480 --> 00:27:28,800
Let's go!

288
00:27:28,880 --> 00:27:30,840
If we don't hurry,
we'll be stuck with leftovers.

289
00:27:36,800 --> 00:27:38,600
You'll suffocate me
before the illness gets me.

290
00:27:42,520 --> 00:27:43,360
Zheng Yu.

291
00:27:43,920 --> 00:27:46,840
We're just classmates hanging out.
Why are you acting so guilty?

292
00:27:47,440 --> 00:27:50,360
If certain people saw us,
who knows what they'd think?

293
00:27:51,120 --> 00:27:52,320
Certain people?

294
00:27:52,400 --> 00:27:53,240
Who?

295
00:27:53,760 --> 00:27:54,640
Xie Yudi?

296
00:28:05,400 --> 00:28:08,840
You were the one who borrowed my equipment
for light trapping yesterday, right?

297
00:28:08,920 --> 00:28:11,440
You were fine yesterday.
How did you get a fever today?

298
00:28:12,080 --> 00:28:13,000
He got caught in the rain.

299
00:28:14,400 --> 00:28:17,360
The hospital is too far from here.
Driving on the mountain roads is tricky.

300
00:28:17,440 --> 00:28:20,040
I'll take you to the local health center
for a checkup first.

301
00:28:20,120 --> 00:28:22,000
- Thank you for your help.
- It's fine.

302
00:28:22,080 --> 00:28:24,160
You two just have terrible timing.

303
00:28:24,240 --> 00:28:27,160
Your group leader, Mr. Sun,
went to a nearby farm restaurant

304
00:28:27,240 --> 00:28:30,280
to catch the students
who sneaked out for a late-night meal.

305
00:28:30,360 --> 00:28:31,360
This isn't like the city.

306
00:28:31,440 --> 00:28:32,640
You can't just hail a cab.

307
00:28:32,720 --> 00:28:35,120
Luckily, I was on night duty.
It's just a quick drive.

308
00:28:37,160 --> 00:28:38,200
Is he okay?

309
00:28:41,840 --> 00:28:44,120
That's how mountain roads are.
They're bumpy when it rains.

310
00:28:44,200 --> 00:28:45,320
Just focus on driving.

311
00:29:38,840 --> 00:29:41,280
WESTERN MEDICINE PHARMACY,
PAYMENTS/BILLING

312
00:29:44,640 --> 00:29:45,480
Doctor.

313
00:29:47,480 --> 00:29:48,520
What's the problem?

314
00:29:48,600 --> 00:29:51,240
He got caught in the rain last night
and developed a fever.

315
00:29:51,320 --> 00:29:53,120
Come with me then.
I'll take your temperature.

316
00:30:01,920 --> 00:30:03,200
It's 38.6 degrees.

317
00:30:03,920 --> 00:30:05,920
I'll give you an IV drip
and prescribe some medicine.

318
00:30:11,200 --> 00:30:12,640
XIE YUDI

319
00:30:15,040 --> 00:30:16,240
Do you have any allergies?

320
00:30:16,960 --> 00:30:20,080
I'm allergic to eggs.
I took some allergy meds for it recently.

321
00:30:20,160 --> 00:30:21,080
What did you take?

322
00:30:25,480 --> 00:30:26,520
All right.

323
00:30:30,800 --> 00:30:32,040
You're allergic to eggs?

324
00:30:36,400 --> 00:30:37,520
I wasn't before.

325
00:30:38,120 --> 00:30:39,640
After I got sick,

326
00:30:40,240 --> 00:30:41,680
I suddenly discovered it one day.

327
00:30:41,760 --> 00:30:43,320
At your house last time,

328
00:30:43,400 --> 00:30:45,320
you seemed to love the scrambled eggs.

329
00:30:47,840 --> 00:30:50,120
We don't waste food in my family.

330
00:30:50,800 --> 00:30:52,000
Chen Yanzhou.

331
00:30:56,560 --> 00:30:57,440
I just…

332
00:30:58,240 --> 00:30:59,760
didn't want to disappoint the cook.

333
00:31:03,320 --> 00:31:05,720
Even if you want to
take care of your sick mom,

334
00:31:05,800 --> 00:31:07,720
you shouldn't treat yourself this way.

335
00:31:11,960 --> 00:31:14,520
By the way, during the game today,

336
00:31:15,520 --> 00:31:16,840
why did you choose Xie Yudi?

337
00:31:18,120 --> 00:31:20,120
I had no idea you two were so close.

338
00:31:24,320 --> 00:31:25,560
I'll take this call.

339
00:31:51,800 --> 00:31:53,240
Lean back and get some rest.

340
00:31:54,640 --> 00:31:56,040
I'm not sleepy.

341
00:31:56,960 --> 00:32:00,120
Besides, someone has to
keep an eye on the IV drip

342
00:32:00,200 --> 00:32:01,520
to see when it finishes.

343
00:32:02,360 --> 00:32:03,280
Don't worry.

344
00:32:03,360 --> 00:32:05,760
I've spoken to the doctor.
He'll keep an eye on it.

345
00:32:06,440 --> 00:32:07,560
Get some sleep.

346
00:32:07,640 --> 00:32:09,120
I have something to do. I'll just--

347
00:32:09,200 --> 00:32:11,720
I understand. Go ahead.

348
00:33:18,800 --> 00:33:20,120
You're awake.

349
00:33:20,200 --> 00:33:22,000
Yes. I'm awake.

350
00:33:22,080 --> 00:33:23,160
You…

351
00:33:26,320 --> 00:33:27,480
Your fever's gone down.

352
00:33:33,800 --> 00:33:35,840
You don't need to take this box.
Take this one instead.

353
00:33:40,520 --> 00:33:42,240
You didn't leave last night?

354
00:33:42,320 --> 00:33:43,360
Leave?

355
00:33:43,440 --> 00:33:44,720
Where would I go?

356
00:33:44,800 --> 00:33:47,920
You took a call yesterday and said
you had to return to the base.

357
00:33:48,000 --> 00:33:49,480
I did get a call.

358
00:33:49,560 --> 00:33:50,960
It was from a biotech company.

359
00:33:51,040 --> 00:33:53,720
They said they had some
urgent documents to translate.

360
00:33:54,640 --> 00:33:57,200
So… you stayed here all night?

361
00:34:02,040 --> 00:34:04,400
It was raining last night,
and the temperature dropped.

362
00:34:04,480 --> 00:34:05,840
Why didn't you sit inside?

363
00:34:06,440 --> 00:34:09,040
I had to call the biotech company
to go over the documents.

364
00:34:09,120 --> 00:34:10,400
I didn't want to disturb you.

365
00:34:12,320 --> 00:34:13,159
Let's go.

366
00:34:13,239 --> 00:34:16,000
Let's get back and grab a bite
before you take your medicine.

367
00:34:32,600 --> 00:34:33,639
Can you believe this?

368
00:34:33,719 --> 00:34:35,880
We've only just got here,
and now we're leaving.

369
00:34:35,960 --> 00:34:37,960
Are we the unluckiest class ever?

370
00:34:38,040 --> 00:34:39,679
Last year, the base was under maintenance.

371
00:34:39,760 --> 00:34:42,480
This year, they scheduled it
to avoid overlapping with the sophomores,

372
00:34:42,560 --> 00:34:44,600
but they got the weather wrong.

373
00:34:45,199 --> 00:34:46,040
Seriously…

374
00:34:46,120 --> 00:34:46,960
Everyone.

375
00:34:47,040 --> 00:34:49,840
Our ride should arrive
in about 40 minutes.

376
00:34:49,920 --> 00:34:52,120
Since the rain has stopped,
let's hurry down the mountain.

377
00:34:52,199 --> 00:34:53,639
Has everyone packed their bags?

378
00:34:53,719 --> 00:34:55,199
- Yes!
- Yes!

379
00:34:55,280 --> 00:34:56,880
Sir, some people are still packing inside.

380
00:34:56,960 --> 00:34:58,360
- They're not done yet?
- Yes.

381
00:34:58,440 --> 00:35:00,280
Come on. Let's go hurry them along.

382
00:35:01,320 --> 00:35:02,920
I don't really want to go back.

383
00:35:17,360 --> 00:35:18,520
<i>Where's your roommate?</i>

384
00:35:18,600 --> 00:35:19,840
<i>Still packing?</i>

385
00:35:24,680 --> 00:35:25,640
What's going on here?

386
00:35:25,720 --> 00:35:27,920
Exactly. Just got back from a walk?

387
00:35:28,000 --> 00:35:31,000
Could they be one of the few who escaped
last night's farmhouse restaurant raid?

388
00:35:31,080 --> 00:35:32,760
They sure know how to hide!

389
00:35:32,840 --> 00:35:35,440
Looks like they were out all night.
They haven't changed clothes.

390
00:35:35,520 --> 00:35:37,320
Isn't that a little too blatant?

391
00:35:37,400 --> 00:35:38,680
You're so clueless.

392
00:35:38,760 --> 00:35:40,760
Those two got together
at the end of last semester.

393
00:35:40,840 --> 00:35:41,720
Can't you tell?

394
00:35:44,000 --> 00:35:44,880
Holy crap!

395
00:35:47,680 --> 00:35:49,560
- Whose car is this?
- Whose car is this?

396
00:35:51,440 --> 00:35:54,000
Don't tell me this is the ride
Mr. Sun arranged for us.

397
00:36:11,360 --> 00:36:12,840
Dad, what are you doing here?

398
00:36:12,920 --> 00:36:15,160
Your group leader told me
everything that happened.

399
00:36:16,400 --> 00:36:17,480
You have to understand.

400
00:36:18,400 --> 00:36:20,680
A high fever can trigger
a recurrence of myocarditis.

401
00:36:20,760 --> 00:36:23,000
Your lecturers were worried
something might happen.

402
00:36:23,720 --> 00:36:25,200
They didn't want to be held responsible.

403
00:36:25,760 --> 00:36:28,160
I've already told you I'm fine.
Feel for yourself.

404
00:36:31,520 --> 00:36:33,640
I still think you're a little warm.

405
00:36:34,760 --> 00:36:36,960
Your hand isn't as reliable
as a hospital thermometer.

406
00:36:37,800 --> 00:36:40,880
Who would've thought?
Chen Yanzhou comes from a rich family.

407
00:36:40,960 --> 00:36:43,560
As if being rich weren't enough,
he gets good grades too.

408
00:36:43,640 --> 00:36:45,560
And girls like him too.

409
00:36:46,240 --> 00:36:47,440
Did you see that?

410
00:36:47,520 --> 00:36:49,520
Chen Yanzhou's dad greeted Zheng Yu.

411
00:36:49,600 --> 00:36:50,560
Did he?

412
00:36:51,720 --> 00:36:54,240
Of course he did!
Those four eyes of yours are useless.

413
00:37:17,960 --> 00:37:20,160
Dr. Lin's specialist appointment
was fully booked today,

414
00:37:20,240 --> 00:37:22,160
so I booked one for tomorrow.

415
00:37:22,240 --> 00:37:23,400
Either way,

416
00:37:24,240 --> 00:37:25,920
you need to get checked.

417
00:37:27,960 --> 00:37:28,800
Got it.

418
00:37:29,400 --> 00:37:30,720
Dad, do you have a charging cable?

419
00:37:30,800 --> 00:37:33,520
Staring at your phone
in the car strains your eyes.

420
00:37:33,600 --> 00:37:35,560
If it's dead, just leave it dead.

421
00:37:36,720 --> 00:37:38,280
I need to let my classmate know.

422
00:37:38,360 --> 00:37:39,720
I left before I could tell them.

423
00:37:40,320 --> 00:37:42,680
What kind of classmate
requires you to report in like this?

424
00:37:44,680 --> 00:37:45,520
Help yourself.

425
00:37:47,360 --> 00:37:49,040
CIGARETTES

426
00:38:04,680 --> 00:38:07,280
What's wrong?
Is your classmate mad at you?

427
00:38:11,000 --> 00:38:12,080
It hasn't even turned on yet.

428
00:38:28,960 --> 00:38:29,840
Are you okay?

429
00:38:30,400 --> 00:38:31,480
I'm fine.

430
00:38:38,920 --> 00:38:40,440
<i>What time did Zheng Yu leave last night?</i>

431
00:38:42,120 --> 00:38:43,080
<i>I'm not sure.</i>

432
00:38:43,160 --> 00:38:44,320
<i>We had a falling out,</i>

433
00:38:44,400 --> 00:38:46,600
<i>so I got back to my room</i>
<i>really late last night.</i>

434
00:38:46,680 --> 00:38:48,040
<i>With a personality like yours,</i>

435
00:38:48,120 --> 00:38:49,800
<i>how do you even manage</i>
<i>to have a falling out?</i>

436
00:38:51,560 --> 00:38:53,840
<i>She thought I was the one</i>
<i>who sent that text.</i>

437
00:38:54,360 --> 00:38:55,920
<i>She thinks I'm disgusting.</i>

438
00:38:57,120 --> 00:38:59,800
<i>So don't ask me about her anymore,</i>

439
00:39:00,440 --> 00:39:02,920
<i>and don't try to use me</i>
<i>to do anything for her either,</i>

440
00:39:03,000 --> 00:39:04,440
<i>because she won't fall for it again.</i>

441
00:39:07,800 --> 00:39:12,360
Everyone, check with your group members
to make sure everyone's here.

442
00:39:12,440 --> 00:39:14,280
Sir, Zhuang Ning is still not here.

443
00:39:16,120 --> 00:39:18,040
Zhuang Ning? Isn't she right over there?

444
00:39:22,240 --> 00:39:23,280
I didn't see her just now.

445
00:39:23,960 --> 00:39:25,520
Okay, sit properly and settle down.

446
00:39:28,800 --> 00:39:29,920
<i>I'm leaving first.</i>

447
00:39:30,000 --> 00:39:30,960
CHEN YANZHOU

448
00:39:37,480 --> 00:39:38,400
They really fell out?

449
00:39:45,640 --> 00:39:48,400
LIYUAN BUILDING 9

450
00:39:51,120 --> 00:39:55,120
Should we explain in more detail
how we identified the insect order?

451
00:39:55,720 --> 00:39:58,320
But too much text will affect the layout.

452
00:39:59,440 --> 00:40:00,680
Linlin.

453
00:40:00,760 --> 00:40:04,320
My report is missing a few insect photos.

454
00:40:04,400 --> 00:40:06,480
Did you take any?
Could you send me a few?

455
00:40:07,760 --> 00:40:09,520
Didn't Zheng Yu do the light trapping?

456
00:40:09,600 --> 00:40:10,800
She should have those photos.

457
00:40:13,640 --> 00:40:16,080
Just leave that part blank.
I'll handle it later.

458
00:40:16,680 --> 00:40:18,120
It's fine. I can finish it myself.

459
00:40:19,360 --> 00:40:22,080
That's Chen Yanzhou's section.
You don't need to do it.

460
00:40:26,320 --> 00:40:27,480
What's going on with them?

461
00:40:31,720 --> 00:40:34,600
Everyone, I have a suggestion.

462
00:40:34,680 --> 00:40:38,520
After our fieldwork presentations,
let's have a dorm dinner together.

463
00:40:39,360 --> 00:40:40,240
My treat!

464
00:40:40,320 --> 00:40:41,320
Sounds good!

465
00:40:41,400 --> 00:40:44,080
Didn't Zhuang Ning say
at the end of last semester

466
00:40:44,160 --> 00:40:45,680
that we'd never had a dorm dinner?

467
00:40:46,760 --> 00:40:49,920
A new place just opened at Paradise Walk.
It's only two stops away.

468
00:40:50,000 --> 00:40:51,720
Why don't we book a table there?

469
00:40:52,560 --> 00:40:54,680
- I'm busy.
- I want to rest after the presentation.

470
00:41:42,160 --> 00:41:43,000
Ms. Yang.

471
00:41:45,440 --> 00:41:46,360
Xiaochen.

472
00:41:53,080 --> 00:41:55,000
What bad timing.

473
00:41:55,080 --> 00:41:56,160
Zheng Yu isn't here today.

474
00:41:57,240 --> 00:41:59,040
I know. I'm not here to see her.

475
00:42:00,280 --> 00:42:02,400
I've caught a bit of a cold,
so I came for medicine.

476
00:42:02,480 --> 00:42:04,440
I happened to see someone drinking this.

477
00:42:10,960 --> 00:42:11,800
There's more.

478
00:42:14,760 --> 00:42:15,720
This…

479
00:42:15,800 --> 00:42:18,400
Please don't tell her.
I don't want her to get the wrong idea.

480
00:42:18,480 --> 00:42:20,880
I brought these for you.
It has nothing to do with her.

481
00:42:20,960 --> 00:42:23,600
Since you put it that way,
I'll keep it a secret.

482
00:42:24,240 --> 00:42:25,440
I need to take a picture.

483
00:42:25,520 --> 00:42:27,280
I was just wondering what to post today.

484
00:42:28,240 --> 00:42:29,640
What do you mean?

485
00:42:29,720 --> 00:42:32,200
I have an account
where I share bits of my life.

486
00:42:32,280 --> 00:42:33,480
I have quite a lot of followers.

487
00:42:37,560 --> 00:42:38,920
Where did my phone go?

488
00:42:42,320 --> 00:42:44,200
I probably left it at the nurses' station.

489
00:42:44,280 --> 00:42:45,880
My memory's getting worse and worse.

490
00:42:45,960 --> 00:42:46,840
Want me to get it--

491
00:42:46,920 --> 00:42:48,640
No, no. You stay there.

492
00:42:48,720 --> 00:42:51,200
I'll get it myself.
We still need to add each other on WeChat.

493
00:42:52,160 --> 00:42:53,000
Sure.

494
00:46:18,360 --> 00:46:23,360
Subtitle translation by: Cempaka Malinja
